Input: {"question": "64th Division was formed in which year?", "original_source_segments": {"D1S1": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0340-bff88b94178c:d00", "start": 0, "end": 136, "text": "64th (2nd Highland) Division The 64th (2nd Highland) Division was an infantry division of the British Army, raised during the Great War."}, "D1S2": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0340-bff88b94178c:d00", "start": 137, "end": 274, "text": "The division was formed in late 1914 as a second-line Territorial Force formation which served on home defence duties throughout the war."}, "D1S3": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0340-bff88b94178c:d00", "start": 275, "end": 453, "text": "The division was formed as a duplicate of the 51st (Highland) Division in 1914, composed primarily of soldiers from Highland regiments recruited in northern and central Scotland."}, "D1S4": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0340-bff88b94178c:d00", "start": 454, "end": 552, "text": "By 1917-18, however, it had become a training unit composed of conscripts from throughout Britain."}, "D1S5": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0340-bff88b94178c:d00", "start": 553, "end": 639, "text": "It remained on home defence and training duties in Scotland and England throughout the"}, "D2S1": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0340-bff88b94178c:d01", "start": 0, "end": 98, "text": "64th Division (Imperial Japanese Army) The was an infantry division of the Imperial Japanese Army."}, "D2S2": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0340-bff88b94178c:d01", "start": 99, "end": 122, "text": "Its call sign was the ."}, "D2S3": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0340-bff88b94178c:d01", "start": 123, "end": 250, "text": "It was formed on 1 May 1943 in Hubei province, simultaneously with the 62nd and 63rd divisions as a security (type C) division."}, "D2S4": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0340-bff88b94178c:d01", "start": 251, "end": 307, "text": "The nucleus for the formation was the 12th from Chuzhou."}, "D2S5": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0340-bff88b94178c:d01", "start": 308, "end": 364, "text": "As a security division, it lacked an artillery regiment."}, "D2S6": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0340-bff88b94178c:d01", "start": 365, "end": 443, "text": "The men of the division were drafted from the Hiroshima mobilization district."}, "D2S7": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0340-bff88b94178c:d01", "start": 444, "end": 509, "text": "On 10 July 1943, the 64th division was assigned to the 20th army."}, "D2S8": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0340-bff88b94178c:d01", "start": 510, "end": 597, "text": "The division was then garrisoned in Yangzhou, Jiangbei District, Ningbo, Zhenjiang, and"}, "D3S1": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0340-bff88b94178c:d02", "start": 0, "end": 6, "text": "Army ."}, "D3S2": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0340-bff88b94178c:d02", "start": 7, "end": 65, "text": "Its call sign was the Open Division ( 開兵団 , Kai Heidan ) ."}, "D3S3": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0340-bff88b94178c:d02", "start": 66, "end": 197, "text": "It was formed on 1 May 1943 in Hubei province , simultaneously with the 62nd and 63rd divisions as a security ( type C ) division ."}, "D3S4": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0340-bff88b94178c:d02", "start": 198, "end": 281, "text": "The nucleus for the formation was the 12th Independent Mixed Brigade from Chuzhou ."}, "D3S5": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0340-bff88b94178c:d02", "start": 282, "end": 340, "text": "As a security division , it lacked an artillery regiment ."}, "D3S6": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0340-bff88b94178c:d02", "start": 341, "end": 420, "text": "The men of the division were drafted from the Hiroshima mobilization district ."}, "D3S7": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0340-bff88b94178c:d02", "start": 421, "end": 504, "text": "Action [ edit ] On 10 July 1943 , the 64th division was assigned to the 20th army ."}, "D4S1": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0340-bff88b94178c:d03", "start": 0, "end": 75, "text": "sending their aircraft to storage, disposal or return to the United States."}, "D4S2": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0340-bff88b94178c:d03", "start": 76, "end": 121, "text": "It was inactivated in Germany on 5 June 1947."}, "D4S3": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0340-bff88b94178c:d03", "start": 122, "end": 248, "text": "Reactivated as an Air Division under Northeast Air Command (NEAC) at Pepperrell Air Force Base, Newfoundland in December 1952."}, "D4S4": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0340-bff88b94178c:d03", "start": 249, "end": 449, "text": "NEAC had taken over the former Newfoundland Base Command atmospheric forces and ground air and radar stations in Newfoundland, Northeastern Canada and Greenland upon the former command's inactivation."}, "D4S5": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0340-bff88b94178c:d03", "start": 450, "end": 540, "text": "The 64th Air Division was NEAC's command and control echelon of command over these assets."}, "D4S6": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0340-bff88b94178c:d03", "start": 541, "end": 665, "text": "\"Its mission was the administration, training and providing air defense combat ready forces within its designated geographic"}, "D5S1": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0340-bff88b94178c:d04", "start": 0, "end": 66, "text": "Squadron , which went to Thule AB , Greenland with four F-94B 's ."}, "D5S2": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0340-bff88b94178c:d04", "start": 67, "end": 218, "text": "Additional interceptor squadrons were established at Goose AFB in Labrador and Ernest Harmon AFB in Newfoundland and were composed of F-94s and F-89s ."}, "D5S3": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0340-bff88b94178c:d04", "start": 219, "end": 471, "text": "Also , there were numerous deployments of fighter-interceptor squadrons from the Tactical Air Command and Air Defense Command to NEAC bases , along with Strategic Air Command tankers and bombers , primarily using Thule as a refueling and staging base ."}, "D5S4": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0340-bff88b94178c:d04", "start": 472, "end": 574, "text": "[ 9 ] Plans were made in 1952 to station anti-aircraft units at Thule for the protection of the base ."}, "D6S1": {"document_number": 6, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0340-bff88b94178c:d05", "start": 0, "end": 574, "text": "Established as the 6th Pursuit Wing on 19 October 1940 Activated on 18 December 1940 Inactivated on 7 December 1941 Redesignated 6th Fighter Wing on 30 May 1942 Activated on 7 June 1942 Disestablished on 13 September 1943 Reestablished on 5 August 1946 Activated on 25 August 1946 Inactivated on 28 July 1948 Redesignated 6th Air Division on 1 February 1951 Organized on 10 February 1951 Discontinued on 16 June 1952 Activated on 16 June 1952 Discontinued and inactivated on 2 July 1966 Activated on 5 July 1968 Organized on 1 August 1968 Inactivated on 15 December 1969 [ 1"}}, "original_cards": [{"doc_id": "ramdocs-0340-bff88b94178c:d00", "card_id": "ramdocs-0340-bff88b94178c:d00:c0", "entity": "64th Division", "scope": "formation year", "claim": "The 64th (2nd Highland) Division was formed in 1914.", "answer": "1914", "quote": "The division was formed in late 1914 as a second-line Territorial Force formation which served on home defence duties throughout the war. The division was formed as a duplicate of the 51st (Highland) Division in 1914, composed primarily of soldiers from Highland regiments recruited in northern and central Scotland.", "original_document_number": 1}, {"doc_id": "ramdocs-0340-bff88b94178c:d01", "card_id": "ramdocs-0340-bff88b94178c:d01:c0", "entity": "64th Division", "scope": "formation year", "claim": "The 64th Division was formed in 1943.", "answer": "1943", "quote": "It was formed on 1 May 1943 in Hubei province, simultaneously with the 62nd and 63rd divisions as a security (type C) division.", "original_document_number": 2}, {"doc_id": "ramdocs-0340-bff88b94178c:d02", "card_id": "ramdocs-0340-bff88b94178c:d02:c0", "entity": "64th Division", "scope": "formation year", "claim": "The 64th Division was formed in 1943.", "answer": "1943", "quote": "It was formed on 1 May 1943 in Hubei province , simultaneously with the 62nd and 63rd divisions as a security ( type C ) division .", "original_document_number": 3}, {"doc_id": "ramdocs-0340-bff88b94178c:d05", "card_id": "ramdocs-0340-bff88b94178c:d05:c0", "entity": "64th Division", "scope": "formation year", "claim": "The 64th Division was formed in 1940.", "answer": "1940", "quote": "Established as the 6th Pursuit Wing on 19 October 1940 Activated on 18 December 1940 Inactivated on 7 December 1941 Redesignated 6th Fighter Wing on 30 May 1942 Activated on 7 June 1942 Disestablished on 13 September 1943 Reestablished on 5 August 1946 Activated on 25 August 1946 Inactivated on 28 July 1948 Redesignated 6th Air Division on 1 February 1951 Organized on 10 February 1951 Discontinued on 16 June 1952 Activated on 16 June 1952 Discontinued and inactivated on 2 July 1966 Activated on 5 July 1968 Organized on 1 August 1968 Inactivated on 15 December 1969 [ 1", "original_document_number": 6}], "current_answers": ["1914", "1943"], "candidate_answers": [{"candidate_id": "R0", "answer": "1914", "origin": "initial"}, {"candidate_id": "R1", "answer": "1943", "origin": "initial"}], "requested_slot_hint": "year"}
